WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.700
Imagine a world without fish.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Without fishing communities.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.500
The bountiful harvests of the sea,

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.200
Have provided so much, to so many, for so long.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.500
Fish and fishing have gone hand in hand with culture,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.000
with prosperity,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
with the very roots of civilisation.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.500
Ever since the birth of humanity

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Our ocean has helped feed us.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.500
It has helped us stay healthy.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.500
Fish consumption around the world has more than doubled

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.000
in the last fifty years.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
But for many, it is far more than a healthy supplement to their diet.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.000
One in ten people depend on seafood for their livelihoods.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:17.000
For one billion people, largely from developing countries, seafood is the primary source of animal protein.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.000
But our ocean has its limits.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Ever growing demand means ever growing pressure on dwindling stocks.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:35.000
Population growth and environmental degradation will make the problem worse.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.000
Action must be taken

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
so that stocks are fished sustainably.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:50.500
We must eradicate Illegal, Unreported and Unregulated fishing

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.500
– accounting for 15% of the world’s catch –

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.500
A global response is needed to clamp down on those who don’t play by the rules.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.000
Hope also comes from aquaculture.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.500
We already eat more fish from aquaculture than from wild fisheries.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.500
Like our ancestors on land, we are moving from hunting to farming.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.500
Whilst strict environmental standards must be met,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.500
Aquaculture can help meet the growing demand for seafood.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.200
So what will we do together to ensure:

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.000
that fisheries are sustainably managed?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.500
that the aquaculture sector grows responsibly?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.200
And that the futures of fish and fishing communities are secured?

